WEBVTT

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.120
The story so far.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.650
Nozomu was caught up in a red-white liberation protest in Kichijoji that began when it was discovered

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.480
that the homeowners association was blocking home construction.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:21.210
Backing an argument that, if red and white were that hated, Kohaku should be cancelled for New Year's,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.890
Aso said “Nerds should be OK with the tricolor.”

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.680
Kohaku had another color mixed in.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:34.120
But the famous enka singers selected for this new “Tea Green” team, neither the familiar red nor white, raged.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.280
Nozomu, his life and chastity threatened, was in a bind...

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.210
Having lived on the run for a year, Nozomu found
himself at a shop called “Allgays 2-chome Sunset”. {ED: what's "2-chome"?}

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.310
A madam resembling Chemistry's
Kawabata says “I preferred the old days.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:51.360
We didn't have cell phones or pearls or beads, but we had dreams!”

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.350
At that moment, an HOA rep appeared
saying “Were you trying to be moving?”!

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.700
On her tea-green armband were the words “Wakakusa Four Sisters”...

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:36.210
It's an Easter egg.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.300
Which came first, the chicken or the egg?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.560
Where are you going?

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:45.720
Do nerds exist because there is anime

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:45.890
Does anime exist because there are nerds

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:46.060
Do I work on this to live

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.220
Do I live to work on this

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:46.390
Are the staff worn out because the schedule is wrecked

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:46.640
Is the schedule wrecked because the staff are worn out

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.490
Which came first, the shut-in or the house?

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.110
The house, of course. Otherwise, they'd have nothing to be shut in.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.980
No, I don't think so.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.560
I think that, long before mankind
began to build houses, shut-ins existed.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.620
In holes in the woods.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.860
In the woods...

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.090
Don't open it.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.260
That's a pretty outdoorsy shut-in.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.090
You're not wearing panties again!

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.520
Aren't you embarrassed!?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.950
Embarrassed?

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.860
Hold on a moment.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.690
This, too, must be questioned.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.050
Which came first, panties or shame?

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.650
I'll sue you!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:47.660
He means, did people start wearing
panties because they were ashamed,

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:53.330
or did people start being ashamed after taking off their panties?

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.820
That's right.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.630
Either way, you're not wearing panties. {*}

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.010
Don't say weird things like that!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.100
Hey, what's wrong?

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.140
For some reason, I suddenly feel ashamed.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.640
You can cover up with this.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.450
I tried putting on a leaf.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.480
For some reason, I can't take it!

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.190
I'm gonna rip it off!

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.030
Stop it! I'm embarrassed!

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.300
Em...barrassed?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.530
Embarrassed?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.240
Yes. In this world,

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:35.710
there are cases, like the chicken and the egg, where one cannot tell which came first.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:41.340
Were special interests born because of Parliament, or was Parliament born because of special interests!?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.050
Are comic books published to sell graphic novels,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.390
or are graphic novels published because issue after issue of the comic piled up?

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.890
Was the company named for the place, or the place named for the company?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.640
Which came first!?

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.610
Which came first, the idol group or the fans?

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.990
You were there?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:05.990
Yes, always.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.450
Which came first, the idol group or the fans?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.400
The idol group came first and then it got fans, right?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.170
Not necessarily.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.800
It's completely plausible for the fans to have come first.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:34.170
If they made an idol group with 48 girls, I'd definitely be a fan.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.560
I'll do it!

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.250
So fans could have come first.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.810
That specific!?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.320
You could say it's precisely because of that kind of needy fan that the group exists.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:51.330
Which came first, S or M?

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.470
Well, I guess they could have happened at the same time.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.060
Do I not get any because I'm a nerd, or did I become a nerd because I wasn't getting any?

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.020
Don't be so naive.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.060
You're a nerd because you're a nerd!

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.520
You're not getting any because you're not getting any!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.220
As well as things where it isn't obvious what came first,

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:33.450
there are things where what came first is well-known but the truth is murkier.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.160
For example, which came first, the 
hamburger steak or the hamburger?

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:39.970
It's gotta be the hamburger steak, no matter how you look at it.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.600
I haff kreated dis ting kalled der hahmburker, {special assignment: hollywood german accent}

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.460
but I vould much like to put zometing betveen it.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.350
Vat if ve place betveen it zome grount meat?

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.590
Du are a jenius!

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.400
Und ve shall kall dis meat die hamburk steak!

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.600
Ja vohl!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.390
For example.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.100
It's just a bun when it's got nothing between it!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.060
There're other examples.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.670
It's tea time, old chap. {here we go again}

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:01.690
Tea time indeed.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.760
I say, do you perhaps feel a trifle parched whilst eating scones?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.350
As if one's mouth were withering.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:12.500
Mayhap 'twould behoove us to place in hot
water some leaves, and henceforth drink it?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.410
Brilliant!

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:16.510
As it is a refreshment for tea time, we shall refer to it as tea!

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:17.120
Indeed!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:22.040
Maybe they made tea because of tea time!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.540
No way!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:29.210
Are you saying that Russians are called
that because they play Russian roulette,

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.480
and that Mongols are called that
because they do Mongolian chops?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:37.140
I'm furious! I met a panty thief!

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.520
Which came first, panties or panty thieves!?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:47.070
Panties came first. Otherwise, there wouldn't be any to steal.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.570
No.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.900
I made something interesting out of a skin.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:53.950
Can we use it for anything?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.450
It's useless.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.410
Oh well. Let's leave it here.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.500
Stop, thief!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.090
What are you even going to use that for after you've stolen it!?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.680
Maybe the panty thief came first, and panties came after!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.830
That's impossible!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:23.870
Well, when they were stolen they were nothing but a weird skin.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.110
Which came first, prostration or the earth's surface?

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.020
Of course, without the earth's surface, it
would be impossible to prostrate oneself.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.010
No, wait.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.360
It burns!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.580
Maybe prostration came first.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.160
Which came first, hope or despair?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.710
Hope came first, of course.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.960
Without hope, you can't feel despair.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.910
I don't understand.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.020
I'm so worn out.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.640
I feel like dying.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.890
I'm in despair.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.560
Don't just despair all the time.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.600
How about having a little hope?

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:08.310
Hope?

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:09.460
Hope?

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:10.330
Hope.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.040
What's hope?

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:15.320
I dunno, it was just on the tip of my tongue.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.400
If I had to think of it, it would be
not despairing, but having wishes...

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.810
Hope.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.030
Hope, huh.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.570
That's a nice word.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.500
What a touching ending.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.640
Japan, a spy's paradise.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:58.210
It is said that twenty thousand operatives of a
certain country have infiltrated modern Japan.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.160
They seek to plunge Japanese society into turmoil.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.080
Keyframer is sick

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:04.290
Animation director can't be found

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:04.450
Assistant director is gone

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:04.620
Both chief animation directors are helping out on Ghostory

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:04.750
An earthquake broke an undersea cable, and the data can't get through

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.080
With Hidamari, Negima, and Ghostory, deadline for delivery is starting to weigh down on us{this is horrible phrasing if the editor ever comes back i'm having him look at it}

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.170
Four, five, six...

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:20.720
Huh, two more yen. I know I have it.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:27.910
Even if she didn't make make such a fuss looking for pocket change, there'd still be a huge line forming behind her.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.440
She's plunging society into turmoil.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:38.210
This must be the work of operatives bent on disturbing our harmonious way of life!

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.660
Now what are you going on about?

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.910
She's just your everyday troublesome person.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:49.110
No, if she's holding up this many people,

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:53.040
it causes an accountable loss.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:57.620
She may be scheming the downfall of Japan as a nation by causing its economy to fall!

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.590
The yen is collapsing!

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.890
That woman may well be an operative!

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.100
If that's true, then isn't this the work of the operatives too?

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.160
Yesterday at the library...

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:21.560
There were people there who were really breaking everyone's concentration.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.320
I didn't think too hard about it at the time, but...

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.070
A couple acting all lovey-dovey at the library...

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:29.620
They must be operatives!

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:34.390
Scheming to weaken the nation's power by lowering the knowledge of the Japanese people!

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.130
Teacher, if that's true, then isn't this the work of operatives too?

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.800
What's up?

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.640
Some idiot clogging things up again.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.470
Pain in the ass.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:56.190
Something like making turnstiles freeze up is the textbook definition of sabotage!

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.920
He must be an operative!

00:11:58.920 --> 00:11:59.940
That's horrible!

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:03.830
Then—!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.990
That must be part of an operative's sabotage activities, too.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:11.860
When someone sitting in front of you has a big head!

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.270
Their objective is to cut off Japan

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:20.300
from the outside world by causing the decline of its anime culture and a decrease in the number of weeaboos!

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:25.510
So many examples come to mind of things which disrupt our harmonious way of life.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.740
Like when someone's ahead of you in line for every ride you go to!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.860
Or when someone changes your bike to the lowest gear while it's locked up!

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:39.360
We encounter their sabotage every day!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.240
It's not writing.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:48.160
I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I must be using it wrong!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.910
Lemme grab that.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.910
I knew it! It was made in that country!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.880
It's a booby trap!

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:59.750
They're building these as a scheme to paralyze Japan's distribution systems!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.630
Such attention to detail...

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.570
You've been in line for a while. Why are you way back there?

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:11.720
I thought I'd make the line shorter for people by leaving.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.830
Next!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.020
Teacher, it's your turn.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.300
You were there?

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.770
Yes, always.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.320
That comes to 315 yen.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.780
All right, three hundred...

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.700
All I've got is a ten-thousand!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.840
Can you break it?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:35.080
Boss! I need change!

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.550
Am I an operative too?

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:51.330
Calling them operatives is strange to begin with. {ED:Mandoric, all I can say is add a TL note. I hate to do it, but holy shit...I'd be reinventing the wheel! Just make life simple...please???}{As in, TL Note: Operative = "one who produces" in jp.}

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.950
What's with operatives <i>destroying</i> things?

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.360
They should make up their minds whether
they're gonna break them or work on them.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:57.480
It's pissing me off!

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:01.150
Real operatives make things, right?

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.320
That's right, Chiri.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.440
Who're they?

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.570
Operatives.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:11.230
It's not like they're here to destroy or sabotage.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.830
They came to Japan to learn how to make things.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.650
Really? What do you want to make?

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:21.500
I would like to make next-generation LCD TVs.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.630
What do you want to make?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:27.180
I would like to make tasty sweet strawberries.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.070
If you're that fired up to learn, I'll teach you!

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.450
I'll pool all my resources and teach you!

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.430
Well...

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.110
They were really operatives!

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.290
Industrial spies!

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:49.210
What are you doing leaking our technology!?

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:50.110
Oh my.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:53.160
You Japanese are too kind.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:57.620
Missiles heaped full of Japanese
engineering are pointed right this way.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:05.180
I feel like, having taught them in good faith, I've been betrayed.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:07.840
Well, don't worry about it too much.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.930
I was naïve.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.520
Upon reflection, I must correct my thinking.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.800
Wow, that's unusual.

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:18.790
I made a big mistake thinking they were operatives who operated on things.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:22.430
I've realized now that they're covert operatives.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:26.650
But if they're trying to be crafty, why
not introduce them to arts and crafts? {i think i saved the whole segment right here.}{EDIT: That's badass. You rock.}

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:33.410
We've invited a special teacher for your crafts class today.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.900
Her name is Miss Kitsu.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.590
All right, class.

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:41.650
Today we'll be studying how to manipulate people through information control.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.260
How about anonymous publications?

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:49.090
That's right. It's a bit old-fashioned, but
anonymous publications are a basic method.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:53.510
Nowadays you can use the internet, too. Though it's easy for you to be tracked, so be careful.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.590
Where's the art in this?

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:57.600
Maybe those submarine blueprints?

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:01.770
Next time, let's study “How to Endure the Rack 101”.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:07.070
There are certainly teachers who are "hard at work” every day. {negative sense---back to the operations/production pun}

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:13.320
For this month's lessons on “operations”, let's go to an amusement park and sketch.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:18.970
100 points.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:19.680
How much can I break labor laws

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:19.840
How far can I stretch the schedule

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:20.010
How short can I cut my sleep schedule

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:20.180
How long can I put off paying my premiums

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:20.340
How little can I pay for food

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:20.600
How much longer can I keep up this line of work, I wonder

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:29.770
What?

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:33.230
How far will shut-ins go to buy Jump?

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:37.470
That's not very much range, even for a shut-in.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.150
Give me a break!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.870
I can at least manage a birdie!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:44.370
By the way, this is how to keep score.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.770
If the <i>zashiki-warashi</i> leaves, the school will crumble!{delrey agreed. lol. probably not the best source when they use -sensei, but.}{ED: wuzzat?}

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:02.000
Oh no, I forgot! Someone stop her!

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:08.500
You all have such amazingly short ranges.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.980
Brother, you've got no room to talk.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.300
There you go.

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:16.980
What's up with this?

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.620
Did I remember to turn off the gas?

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:28.670
Did I turn it off!?

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:31.120
Oh my. You don't have any range at all.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.980
I've double-checked, so I'm fine now.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.590
This time I'll get a lot further.

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:45.260
Did I lock the front door!?

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.560
I knew you wouldn't make it.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.020
I'm just nervous about it!

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:53.060
Everyone just has their own personal ranges.{*}

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.520
What's your range!?

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:58.530
If it's like drivers in golf,

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:05.320
it's best to get as close as possible on the approach shot.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:07.200
As close as possible?

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.790
That man's got a nice close approach.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.290
How much adultery can you commit nearby!?

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.420
That's a bit close.

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:22.980
Real go-getter wives do it when their husbands are gone! They do it right at home; that's a nice approach!

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.800
That's a hole-in-one!

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.260
There're things where you can't have a close approach!

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:33.600
Right now, I'm closest to the pin.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.400
No, I'm closest to the pin.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.120
When did you—!?

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:43.670
I knew this was why a bed I didn't
order got delivered a few days ago!

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:44.870
Closeness.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.660
No matter how physically close you are, it doesn't matter.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.870
You've got to be close psychologically.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.390
I'm closest to the pin.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.120
That's dangerous.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.760
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.050
Matching the song, let's draw illustrations, okay?

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:18.970
Yo, yo, a tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:25.410
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:26.920
The eel...

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.570
Grins!

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:30.120
Lightning...

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.810
Flash!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:35.150
The rain comes pouring down.

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:38.390
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:38.390
Hurry!

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:40.870
Two puddles were made.

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:41.660
Too big!

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:44.520
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:49.050
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:52.570
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.500
Did everyone draw well?

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.600
Bye bye!

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:02.850
Good morning!

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:09.570
On this program, we respond to the
viewers' various opinions and criticisms

00:22:09.570 --> 00:22:11.070
of Zan Sayonara, Zetsubou-sensei.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:13.130
This is the first letter.

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:16.080
These are the thoughts of “Kumagoro” from Tokyo.

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.340
{sign}Making the third season true to the original, whether it's good or bad, is too cautious.

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.080
Can't you be more experimental?

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:24.290
The experimental eps in S2 were great.

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.540
Thanks for your thoughts.

00:22:26.540 --> 00:22:31.550
Producer Miyamoto Junnosuke would like to give a positive response to this thought.

00:22:31.890 --> 00:22:36.940
It the process of producing Zan Sayonara, Zetsubou-sensei, we have attempted to incorporate all your ideas,

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:39.810
and hope that you will continue to be so helpful in future projects.

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.580
Let's move on to the next letter.

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:44.060
This is from “MAEDAX R”.

00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:48.150
{sign}C-part of ep 4 had a huge flashback. Wasn't there enough to work with?

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:50.400
Thanks for your thoughts!

00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:53.640
In response to this, Producer Miyamoto Junnosuke says

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:59.000
there's plenty of anime getting rave reviews, like Evangelion: 2.0 You Can (Not) Advance,

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.410
so you can go watch those.

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:05.000
We don't have time to read all the letters we've received on the air,

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:07.420
but here's a sampling of them.

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.890
You say you're staying true to the original but you're going in completely different directions sometimes.

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:12.240
The DVDs aren't gonna sell.

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:15.080
Of all the places to play around, why the ending credits?

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:16.770
There won't be a fourth season, will there?

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:19.140
And many thoughts like those.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:22.470
Thank you all so much for your thoughts.

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:26.070
Moving on, having considered your thoughts,

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:29.090
we would like to use them in further production.

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:33.400
Please continue supporting Zan, Sayonara Zetsubou-sensei.
